# Token economy

## Read narrow

- Prefer `Grep` or path-scoped search before opening files.
- On large files, use `Read` with offset/limit. Do not open whole trees “just in case.”

## Logs

- On failure, extract the error message and relevant stack only.
- Do not paste or re-read entire terminal or build logs into the thread.

## Stop thrashing

- After two failed approaches on the same failure, stop.
- Summarize what was tried and ask or propose a reset instead of another blind retry.

## Scope replies

- Do not restate full file contents in chat; cite short ranges.
- Prefer diffs over full rewrites when explaining.

## Done metric

- For non-trivial behavior changes, define or update the colocated Vitest assertion before or with the implementation (see project test rules).
